  # DF: /flowKnockoutOtherCoverageWholeYear
  output ko_other_coverage_whole_year condition
  # DF: /flowKnockoutMaritalChangeAffectsContributionLimit
  output ko_marital_change_affects_contribution_limit condition
  # DF: /flowKnockoutMadeQualifiedHsaFundingDistribution
  output ko_made_qualified_hsa_funding_distribution condition
  # DF: /flowKnockoutHsaTestingPeriodAdditionalIncomeYes
  output ko_hsa_testing_period_additional_income_yes condition
  # DF: /knockoutNoPaymentsHsaDistribution
  output ko_no_payments_hsa_distribution condition
  # DF: /flowKnockoutNotEnrolledInHdhp
  output ko_not_enrolled_in_hdhp condition
  # DF: /flowKnockoutEnrolledInMedicareAllYear
  output ko_enrolled_in_medicare_all_year condition
  # DF: /flowKnockoutHsaCoverageChanging
  output ko_hsa_coverage_changing condition
  # DF: /flowKnockoutHsaSelfAndFamilyCoverage
  output ko_hsa_self_and_family_coverage condition
  # DF: /flowKnockoutHdhpCoverageNotAllYear
  output ko_hdhp_coverage_not_all_year condition
  # DF: /flowKnockoutHsaCoverage
  output ko_hsa_coverage condition
  # DF: /flowKnockoutContributionSummaryNoneAllowed
  output ko_contribution_summary_none_allowed condition
  # DF: /flowKnockoutHdhpCoverageStatusNotNeeded
  output ko_hdhp_coverage_status_not_needed condition
  # DF: /hasHsaDistributionsWithoutActivity (BlockSubmissionOnTrue)
  output ko_has_hsa_distributions_without_activity condition
  # DF: /hsaDistributions/secondaryFilerUsedWithoutMFJ (BlockSubmissionOnTrue)
  output ko_hsa_distributions_secondary_filer_used_without_mfj condition
  output unsupported condition
```

## Setup

```catala
scope HsaDistributionItem:
  definition filer equals distribution.filer
  # DF: hsa.xml /hsaDistributions/*/distributionsRolloverAmount
  definition distributions_rollover_amount equals
    if distribution.writable_distributions_rollover_bool
    then distribution.writable_distributions_rollover_amount
    else $0
  # DF: hsa.xml /hsaDistributions/*/withdrawnExcessContributionsAmount
  definition withdrawn_excess_contributions_amount equals
    if distribution.has_withdrawn_excess_contributions
    then distribution.writable_withdrawn_excess_contributions_amount
    else $0
  # DF: hsa.xml /hsaDistributions/*/modifiedDistribution
  definition modified_distribution equals
    distribution.writable_gross_distribution
    - (distributions_rollover_amount + withdrawn_excess_contributions_amount)
  definition gross_distribution equals distribution.writable_gross_distribution
  definition qualified_med_expenses equals
    distribution.writable_qualified_med_expenses
  rule has_earnings_on_excess_contributions under condition
    distribution.writable_earnings_on_excess_contributions > $0
  consequence fulfilled
  rule code_is_not_normal under condition
    distribution.hsa_distribution_code != NormalDistribution
  consequence fulfilled
  rule has_fmv_on_date_of_death under condition
    distribution.writable_fmv_on_date_of_death > $0
  consequence fulfilled
  # The modified distribution above the qualified medical expenses.
  rule has_unqualified_distribution under condition
    modified_distribution > distribution.writable_qualified_med_expenses
  consequence fulfilled

scope Hsa:
  definition is_primary of role equals role = Types.FilerRole.PrimaryFiler
  definition is_secondary of role equals not (is_primary of role)
  definition answers of role equals
    if is_primary of role then primary_filer else secondary_filer
  definition age55_or_older of role equals
    if is_primary of role then primary_filer_age55_or_older
    else secondary_filer_age55_or_older
  definition can_be_claimed of role equals
    if is_primary of role then primary_filer_can_be_claimed
    else secondary_filer_can_be_claimed
  definition items equals
    map each d among hsa_distributions to
      (output of HsaDistributionItem with { -- distribution: d })
```

## 26 U.S.C. § 223: who has HSA activity

The questionnaire asks about contributions that are not on a W-2 and decides
which filers get a Form 8889. Form 8889 instructions, "Who Must File"
(`i8889--2024.pdf` p 3): "You must file Form 8889 if any of the following
applies. You (or someone on your behalf, including your employer) made
contributions for 2024 to your HSA. You received HSA distributions in 2024.
You must include certain amounts in income because you failed to be an
eligible individual during the testing period."

DF writes a screen flow as facts. Where DF's `Switch` has no default (the
answer is only asked under a condition, and is otherwise incomplete), the
answer counts as false here (CONVENTIONS section 3).

```catala
scope Hsa:
  # DF: hsa.xml /flowShowHsaYesNo
  definition flow_show_hsa_yes_no equals
    not has_primary_filer_hsa_contributions_from_w2s
    or (is_filing_status_mfj and not has_secondary_filer_hsa_contributions_from_w2s)
  # DF: hsa.xml /someFilerHadNonEmployerHsaActivity
  definition some_filer_had_non_employer_hsa_activity equals
    flow_show_hsa_yes_no and some_filer_had_non_w2_hsa_activity
  # DF: hsa.xml /flowShowHsaPrimaryYesNo
  definition flow_show_hsa_primary_yes_no equals
    some_filer_had_non_employer_hsa_activity
    and not has_primary_filer_hsa_contributions_from_w2s
  # DF: hsa.xml /primaryFilerHadNonW2HsaActivity
  definition primary_filer_had_non_w2_hsa_activity equals
    flow_show_hsa_primary_yes_no
    and writable_primary_filer_had_non_w2_hsa_activity
  # DF: hsa.xml /flowShowHsaSecondaryYesNo
  definition flow_show_hsa_secondary_yes_no equals
    is_filing_status_mfj and flow_show_hsa_yes_no
    and some_filer_had_non_employer_hsa_activity
    and not has_secondary_filer_hsa_contributions_from_w2s
  # DF: hsa.xml /secondaryFilerHadNonW2HsaActivity
  definition secondary_filer_had_non_w2_hsa_activity equals
    flow_show_hsa_secondary_yes_no
    and writable_secondary_filer_had_non_w2_hsa_activity

  # DF: hsa.xml /filers/*/mayHaveHsaContributionsNotConsideringKos
  definition may_have_hsa_contributions_not_considering_kos of role equals
    (is_filing_status_mfj and is_secondary of role
     and (has_secondary_filer_hsa_contributions_from_w2s
          or (secondary_filer_had_non_w2_hsa_activity
              and some_filer_had_non_employer_hsa_activity)))
    or (is_primary of role
        and (has_primary_filer_hsa_contributions_from_w2s
             or (primary_filer_had_non_w2_hsa_activity
                 and some_filer_had_non_employer_hsa_activity)))
  # DF: hsa.xml /someFilerHasSomeHsaActivityNotConsideringKos
  definition some_filer_has_some_hsa_activity_not_considering_kos equals
    (may_have_hsa_contributions_not_considering_kos of Types.FilerRole.PrimaryFiler)
    or (may_have_hsa_contributions_not_considering_kos of Types.FilerRole.SecondaryFiler)
```

### Medical savings account and excess contributions from earlier years

Form 8889 instructions p 4: "Before you begin: Complete Form 8853, Archer MSAs
and Long-Term Care Insurance Contracts, if required" (`f8889--2024.pdf` p 1).
The Archer MSA (line 4) and prior-year excess contributions (instructions
"Prior Year Excess Contributions", `i8889--2024.pdf` p 8) are not supported.

```catala
scope Hsa:
  # DF: hsa.xml /hasHsaMedicalSavingsAccountTypeDerived
  definition has_hsa_medical_savings_account_type_derived equals
    some_filer_has_some_hsa_activity_not_considering_kos
    and has_hsa_medical_savings_account_type
  # DF: hsa.xml /flowToExcessContributionsPreviousYear
  definition flow_to_excess_contributions_previous_year equals
    some_filer_has_some_hsa_activity_not_considering_kos
    and not has_hsa_medical_savings_account_type
  # DF: hsa.xml /hasHsaExcessContributionsPreviousYear
  definition has_hsa_excess_contributions_previous_year equals
    flow_to_excess_contributions_previous_year
    and writable_has_hsa_excess_contributions_previous_year
  # DF: hsa.xml /flowToHsaExcessContributions (/skipToHsaExcessContributions
  # is complete only on this branch)
  definition flow_to_hsa_excess_contributions equals
    flow_to_excess_contributions_previous_year
    and not writable_has_hsa_excess_contributions_previous_year
  # DF: hsa.xml /hasHsaWithdrawnExcessContributionsYesNo
  definition has_hsa_withdrawn_excess_contributions_yes_no equals
    flow_to_hsa_excess_contributions
    and writable_has_hsa_withdrawn_excess_contributions_yes_no

  # DF: hsa.xml /flowKnockoutHsaExcessContributions
  rule ko_hsa_excess_contributions under condition
    has_hsa_excess_contributions_previous_year
    or has_hsa_withdrawn_excess_contributions_yes_no
  consequence fulfilled
  # DF: hsa.xml /flowKnockoutHsaMedicalSavingsAccountType
  rule ko_hsa_medical_savings_account_type under condition
    (not flow_to_excess_contributions_previous_year)
    and (not flow_to_hsa_excess_contributions)
    and has_hsa_medical_savings_account_type_derived
  consequence fulfilled

  # DF: hsa.xml /filers/*/mayHaveHsaContributions
  definition may_have_hsa_contributions of role equals
    (may_have_hsa_contributions_not_considering_kos of role)
    and not ko_hsa_excess_contributions
    and not ko_hsa_medical_savings_account_type
```

### Contributions made: who has a Part I

```catala
scope Hsa:
  # DF: hsa.xml /filers/*/primaryFilerMayHaveOnlyNonW2Contributions
  definition primary_filer_may_have_only_non_w2_contributions of role equals
    (may_have_hsa_contributions of role)
    and not has_primary_filer_hsa_contributions_from_w2s
    and is_primary of role
  # DF: hsa.xml /filers/*/primaryFilerHasNonW2ContributionsInTy
  definition primary_filer_has_non_w2_contributions_in_ty of role equals
    (primary_filer_may_have_only_non_w2_contributions of role)
    and (answers of role).writable_primary_filer_has_made_contributions_to_hsa
  # DF: hsa.xml /flowSecondaryFilerHasNoHsaContributionsOnW2andMFJ
  definition flow_secondary_filer_has_no_hsa_contributions_on_w2_and_mfj equals
    (may_have_hsa_contributions of Types.FilerRole.SecondaryFiler)
    and not has_secondary_filer_hsa_contributions_from_w2s
    and is_filing_status_mfj
  # DF: hsa.xml /filers/*/secondaryFilerMayHaveOnlyNonW2Contributions
  definition secondary_filer_may_have_only_non_w2_contributions of role equals
    flow_secondary_filer_has_no_hsa_contributions_on_w2_and_mfj
    and is_secondary of role
  # DF: hsa.xml /filers/*/secondaryFilerHasNonW2ContributionsInTy
  definition secondary_filer_has_non_w2_contributions_in_ty of role equals
    (secondary_filer_may_have_only_non_w2_contributions of role)
    and (answers of role).writable_secondary_filer_has_made_contributions_to_hsa
  # DF: hsa.xml /filers/*/flowSkipToHsaTestingPeriodContributionCheck
  definition flow_skip_to_hsa_testing_period_contribution_check of role equals
    ((primary_filer_may_have_only_non_w2_contributions of role)
     and not (primary_filer_has_non_w2_contributions_in_ty of role))
    or ((secondary_filer_may_have_only_non_w2_contributions of role)
        and not (secondary_filer_has_non_w2_contributions_in_ty of role))
  # DF: hsa.xml /filers/*/primaryFilerHasMadeContributionsToHsa
  definition primary_filer_has_made_contributions_to_hsa of role equals
    (may_have_hsa_contributions of role)
    and not (flow_skip_to_hsa_testing_period_contribution_check of role)
    and (has_primary_filer_hsa_contributions_from_w2s
         or (primary_filer_has_non_w2_contributions_in_ty of role))
  # DF: hsa.xml /filers/*/secondaryFilerHasMadeContributionsToHsa
  definition secondary_filer_has_made_contributions_to_hsa of role equals
    (may_have_hsa_contributions of role)
    and not (flow_skip_to_hsa_testing_period_contribution_check of role)
    and (has_secondary_filer_hsa_contributions_from_w2s
         or (secondary_filer_has_non_w2_contributions_in_ty of role))
  # DF: hsa.xml /filers/*/hasMadeContributionsToHsa
  definition has_made_contributions_to_hsa of role equals
    ((is_primary of role) and (primary_filer_has_made_contributions_to_hsa of role))
    or ((is_secondary of role)
        and (secondary_filer_has_made_contributions_to_hsa of role))
  # DF: hsa.xml /bothFilersHaveHsa
  definition both_filers_have_hsa equals
    (has_made_contributions_to_hsa of Types.FilerRole.PrimaryFiler)
    and (has_made_contributions_to_hsa of Types.FilerRole.SecondaryFiler)

  # IRC 223(b)(6): "No deduction shall be allowed under this section to any
  # individual with respect to whom a deduction under section 151 is allowable
  # to another taxpayer". DF: hsa.xml
  # /flowKnockoutFilerIsDependentAndContributesToHsa
  rule ko_filer_is_dependent_and_contributes_to_hsa under condition
    ((has_made_contributions_to_hsa of Types.FilerRole.PrimaryFiler)
     and (can_be_claimed of Types.FilerRole.PrimaryFiler))
    or ((has_made_contributions_to_hsa of Types.FilerRole.SecondaryFiler)
        and (can_be_claimed of Types.FilerRole.SecondaryFiler))
  consequence fulfilled
```

## 26 U.S.C. § 223(b): eligibility, coverage and the limits

### (7) Medicare eligible individuals

"The limitation under this subsection for any month with respect to an
individual shall be zero for the first month such individual is entitled to
benefits under title XVIII of the Social Security Act and for each month
thereafter." A filer on Medicare for part of the year needs the month-by-month
limit, which is not supported; a filer on Medicare all year has no limit.

```catala
scope Hsa:
  # DF: hsa.xml /filers/*/enrolledInMedicarePartOfYearKnockout
  definition enrolled_in_medicare_part_of_year_knockout of role equals
    (has_made_contributions_to_hsa of role)
    and (answers of role).enrolled_in_medicare = MedicarePartOfYear
  # DF: hsa.xml /filers/*/enrolledInMedicareAllYearKnockout
  definition enrolled_in_medicare_all_year_knockout of role equals
    (has_made_contributions_to_hsa of role)
    and (answers of role).enrolled_in_medicare = MedicareAllYear
  # DF: hsa.xml /flowKnockoutHsaCoverageChanging (Medicare changing)
  rule ko_hsa_coverage_changing under condition
    (enrolled_in_medicare_part_of_year_knockout of Types.FilerRole.PrimaryFiler)
    or (enrolled_in_medicare_part_of_year_knockout of Types.FilerRole.SecondaryFiler)
  consequence fulfilled
  # DF: hsa.xml /flowKnockoutEnrolledInMedicareAllYear
  rule ko_enrolled_in_medicare_all_year under condition
    (enrolled_in_medicare_all_year_knockout of Types.FilerRole.PrimaryFiler)
    or (enrolled_in_medicare_all_year_knockout of Types.FilerRole.SecondaryFiler)
  consequence fulfilled
  # DF: hsa.xml /flowKnockoutHdhpCoverageStatusNotNeeded
  rule ko_hdhp_coverage_status_not_needed under condition
    ko_hsa_coverage_changing or ko_enrolled_in_medicare_all_year
  consequence fulfilled
```

### (c)(1) Eligible individual: high deductible health plan coverage

"The term "eligible individual" means, with respect to any month, any
individual if such individual is covered under a high deductible health plan
as of the 1st day of such month, and such individual is not, while covered
under a high deductible health plan, covered under any health plan which is
not a high deductible health plan, and which provides coverage for any benefit
which is covered under the high deductible health plan."

DF supports only a filer who was an eligible individual in every month (the
full-year limit of paragraph (2)); every other coverage answer is a knockout.

```catala
scope Hsa:
  # DF: hsa.xml /filers/*/hsaHdhpCoverageStatusDerived is complete
  definition hsa_hdhp_coverage_status_asked of role equals
    (has_made_contributions_to_hsa of role)
    and not ko_hdhp_coverage_status_not_needed
  # DF: hsa.xml /filers/*/hasHdhpCoverageAllYear
  definition has_hdhp_coverage_all_year of role equals
    (hsa_hdhp_coverage_status_asked of role)
    and (answers of role).hsa_hdhp_coverage_status = HdhpAllYear
  # DF: hsa.xml /filers/*/notEnrolledInHdhpKnockout
  definition not_enrolled_in_hdhp_knockout of role equals
    (hsa_hdhp_coverage_status_asked of role)
    and (answers of role).hsa_hdhp_coverage_status = HdhpNoneOfYear
  # DF: hsa.xml /filers/*/hsaHdhpCoverageStatusKnockout
  definition hsa_hdhp_coverage_status_knockout of role equals
    (hsa_hdhp_coverage_status_asked of role)
    and (answers of role).hsa_hdhp_coverage_status = HdhpPartOfYear
  # DF: hsa.xml /flowKnockoutNotEnrolledInHdhp
  rule ko_not_enrolled_in_hdhp under condition
    (not_enrolled_in_hdhp_knockout of Types.FilerRole.PrimaryFiler)
    or (not_enrolled_in_hdhp_knockout of Types.FilerRole.SecondaryFiler)
  consequence fulfilled
  # DF: hsa.xml /flowKnockoutHdhpCoverageNotAllYear
  rule ko_hdhp_coverage_not_all_year under condition
    (hsa_hdhp_coverage_status_knockout of Types.FilerRole.PrimaryFiler)
    or (hsa_hdhp_coverage_status_knockout of Types.FilerRole.SecondaryFiler)
  consequence fulfilled

  # DF: hsa.xml /filers/*/flowShouldAskForHsaHdhpCoverageType
  definition flow_should_ask_for_hsa_hdhp_coverage_type of role equals
    not ko_hsa_coverage_changing and not ko_not_enrolled_in_hdhp
    and (has_hdhp_coverage_all_year of role)
  # DF: hsa.xml /filers/*/typeOfHdhpKnockout
  definition type_of_hdhp_knockout of role equals
    (flow_should_ask_for_hsa_hdhp_coverage_type of role)
    and (answers of role).type_of_hdhp = BothSelfAndFamily
  # DF: hsa.xml /filers/*/hasSelfOnlyHdhp
  definition has_self_only_hdhp of role equals
    (flow_should_ask_for_hsa_hdhp_coverage_type of role)
    and (answers of role).type_of_hdhp = SelfOnly
  # DF: hsa.xml /filers/*/hasFamilyHdhp
  definition has_family_hdhp of role equals
    (flow_should_ask_for_hsa_hdhp_coverage_type of role)
    and (answers of role).type_of_hdhp = Family
  # DF: hsa.xml /flowKnockoutHsaSelfAndFamilyCoverage
  rule ko_hsa_self_and_family_coverage under condition
    (type_of_hdhp_knockout of Types.FilerRole.PrimaryFiler)
    or (type_of_hdhp_knockout of Types.FilerRole.SecondaryFiler)
  consequence fulfilled

  # DF: hsa.xml /filers/*/flowShouldAskHadCoverageIneligibleForHSAContributions
  definition flow_should_ask_had_coverage_ineligible_for_hsa_contributions
    of role equals
    (flow_should_ask_for_hsa_hdhp_coverage_type of role)
    and ((has_self_only_hdhp of role) or (has_family_hdhp of role))
  # DF: hsa.xml /filers/*/causesOtherCoveragePartOfYearKnockOut
  definition causes_other_coverage_part_of_year_knock_out of role equals
    (flow_should_ask_had_coverage_ineligible_for_hsa_contributions of role)
    and (answers of role).had_other_coverage_ineligible_for_hsa
        = OtherCoveragePartOfYear
  # DF: hsa.xml /filers/*/causesOtherCoverageWholeYearKnockOut
  definition causes_other_coverage_whole_year_knock_out of role equals
    (flow_should_ask_had_coverage_ineligible_for_hsa_contributions of role)
    and (answers of role).had_other_coverage_ineligible_for_hsa
        = OtherCoverageWholeYear
  # DF: hsa.xml /flowKnockoutOtherCoveragePartOfYear
  rule ko_other_coverage_part_of_year under condition
    (causes_other_coverage_part_of_year_knock_out of Types.FilerRole.PrimaryFiler)
    or (causes_other_coverage_part_of_year_knock_out of Types.FilerRole.SecondaryFiler)
  consequence fulfilled
  # DF: hsa.xml /flowKnockoutOtherCoverageWholeYear
  rule ko_other_coverage_whole_year under condition
    (causes_other_coverage_whole_year_knock_out of Types.FilerRole.PrimaryFiler)
    or (causes_other_coverage_whole_year_knock_out of Types.FilerRole.SecondaryFiler)
  consequence fulfilled

  # DF: hsa.xml /flowKnockoutHsaCoverage
  rule ko_hsa_coverage under condition
    ko_hsa_coverage_changing or ko_hsa_self_and_family_coverage
    or ko_hdhp_coverage_not_all_year or ko_other_coverage_part_of_year
  consequence fulfilled
  # DF: hsa.xml /flowKnockoutContributionSummaryNoneAllowed
  rule ko_contribution_summary_none_allowed under condition
    ko_enrolled_in_medicare_all_year or ko_not_enrolled_in_hdhp
    or ko_other_coverage_whole_year
  consequence fulfilled
```

### (5) Special rule for married individuals

"In the case of individuals who are married to each other, if either spouse
has family coverage both spouses shall be treated as having only such family
coverage". Form 8889 instructions, line 1 (`i8889--2024.pdf` p 4): "If you and
your spouse are considered covered by a family HDHP, you are considered
covered by a family HDHP regardless of whether you file jointly or
separately."

DF applies the rule only to a joint return on which the answers of both
spouses are known. For a married filer who is not filing jointly and has
family coverage, the instructions' line 6 steps depend on the spouse's HSA,
which DF does not ask; it knocks the filer out (`ko_mfs_line6_check`).

```catala
scope Hsa:
  # DF: hsa.xml /hsaMarriedFilersHaveFamilyCoverage
  definition hsa_married_filers_have_family_coverage equals
    (flow_should_ask_for_hsa_hdhp_coverage_type of Types.FilerRole.PrimaryFiler)
    and (flow_should_ask_for_hsa_hdhp_coverage_type of Types.FilerRole.SecondaryFiler)
    and is_filing_status_mfj
    and ((has_family_hdhp of Types.FilerRole.PrimaryFiler)
         or (has_family_hdhp of Types.FilerRole.SecondaryFiler))
  # DF: hsa.xml /filers/*/isCoveredByFamilyHdhp
  definition is_covered_by_family_hdhp of role equals
    hsa_married_filers_have_family_coverage or (has_family_hdhp of role)
  # DF: hsa.xml /filers/*/isCoveredBySelfOnlyHdhp
  definition is_covered_by_self_only_hdhp of role equals
    not (is_covered_by_family_hdhp of role) and (has_self_only_hdhp of role)

  # DF: hsa.xml /filers/*/wasEligibleToMakeHsaContributionsAllYear
  # ("Rule of last year does not apply"). DF's
  # /filers/*/hadCoverageDisqualifyingHsaContributions is the constant false
  # and is omitted. IRC 223(b)(6) (dependents) and (b)(7) (Medicare) enter here.
  definition was_eligible_to_make_hsa_contributions_all_year of role equals
    (has_hdhp_coverage_all_year of role)
    and (has_made_contributions_to_hsa of role)
    and (answers of role).enrolled_in_medicare = MedicareNoneOfYear
    and not (can_be_claimed of role)

  # DF: hsa.xml /filers/*/flowShowHsaMfsLine6Check, /filers/*/mfsLine6Check
  # and /flowKnockoutMFSLine6Check (the primary filer's answer)
  rule ko_mfs_line6_check under condition
    is_married and not is_filing_status_mfj
    and (flow_should_ask_for_hsa_hdhp_coverage_type of Types.FilerRole.PrimaryFiler)
    and (has_family_hdhp of Types.FilerRole.PrimaryFiler)
    and primary_filer.writable_mfs_line6_check
  consequence fulfilled

  # DF: hsa.xml /filers/*/checkForChangeInMaritalStatusDuringTaxYear,
  # /filers/*/flowShouldAskForChangeInMaritalStatusDuringTaxYear,
  # /filers/*/changeInMaritalStatusDuringTaxYear,
  # /filers/*/causesMaritalChangeAffectsContributionLimitKnockout and
  # /flowKnockoutMaritalChangeAffectsContributionLimit
  definition causes_marital_change_affects_contribution_limit_knockout
    of role equals
    (has_made_contributions_to_hsa of role)
    and not is_single
    and (if flow_should_ask_had_coverage_ineligible_for_hsa_contributions of role
         then (answers of role).had_other_coverage_ineligible_for_hsa
              = OtherCoverageNoneOfYear
         else true)
    and (answers of role).writable_change_in_marital_status_during_tax_year
        = WasMarriedOrDivorcedThisYear
    and (answers of role).writable_marital_change_affect_contribution_limit_bool
  rule ko_marital_change_affects_contribution_limit under condition
    (causes_marital_change_affects_contribution_limit_knockout
       of Types.FilerRole.PrimaryFiler)
    or (causes_marital_change_affects_contribution_limit_knockout
          of Types.FilerRole.SecondaryFiler)
  consequence fulfilled

  # Form 8889 line 10, qualified HSA funding distributions, is not supported.
  # DF: hsa.xml /filers/*/hasMadeQualifiedHsaFundingDistributionDerived and
  # /flowKnockoutMadeQualifiedHsaFundingDistribution
  rule ko_made_qualified_hsa_funding_distribution under condition
    ((has_made_contributions_to_hsa of Types.FilerRole.PrimaryFiler)
     and primary_filer.has_made_qualified_hsa_funding_distribution)
    or ((has_made_contributions_to_hsa of Types.FilerRole.SecondaryFiler)
        and secondary_filer.has_made_qualified_hsa_funding_distribution)
  consequence fulfilled
```

### (b)(8) Last-month rule and the testing period

"If, at any time during the testing period, the individual is not an eligible
individual, then gross income of the individual for the taxable year in which
occurs the first month in the testing period for which such individual is not
an eligible individual is increased ..." Form 8889 Part III is not supported:
a filer who answers that the last-month rule added income is knocked out.

```catala
scope Hsa:
  # DF: hsa.xml /filers/*/hasToShowTestingPeriodCheck
  definition has_to_show_testing_period_check of role equals
    ((is_primary of role or (is_secondary of role and is_filing_status_mfj))
     and (flow_skip_to_hsa_testing_period_contribution_check of role))
    or ((is_primary of role or (is_secondary of role and is_filing_status_mfj))
        and flow_show_hsa_yes_no and some_filer_had_non_employer_hsa_activity
        and not (may_have_hsa_contributions of role))
  # DF: hsa.xml /flowKnockoutHsaTestingPeriodAdditionalIncomeYes
  rule ko_hsa_testing_period_additional_income_yes under condition
    ((has_to_show_testing_period_check of Types.FilerRole.PrimaryFiler)
     or (has_to_show_testing_period_check of Types.FilerRole.SecondaryFiler))
    and some_filers_made_testing_period_contribution
    and some_filers_have_testing_period_additional_income
  consequence fulfilled
```

## 26 U.S.C. § 223(b): the limit (Form 8889 lines 2 to 13)

### Line 2: contributions you made

Form 8889, line 2: "HSA contributions you made for 2024 (or those made on
your behalf), including those made by the unextended due date of your tax
return that were for 2024. Do not include employer contributions,
contributions through a cafeteria plan, or rollovers." The two inputs are the
contributions made in the year and those made for the year by April 15, 2025
(`i8889--2024.pdf` p 4, line 2).

```catala
scope Hsa:
  # DF: hsa.xml /filers/*/hsaNonemployerContributionsTotal.
  # DF-BUG(4): DF rounds each of the two writable amounts to the dollar and
  # then adds them. The Form 1040 instructions (i1040gi--2024.pdf p 23) say to
  # "include cents when adding the amounts and round off only the total", so
  # the sum is rounded once. Differs only when the two amounts carry cents.
  definition hsa_nonemployer_contributions_total of role equals
    if has_made_contributions_to_hsa of role
    then R.round_dollar of
      ((answers of role).writable_hsa_nonemployer_contributions_tax_year
       + (answers of role).writable_hsa_nonemployer_contributions_tax_year_plus_one)
    else $0
```

### Line 3: the annual limitation

"(2) Monthly limitation. The monthly limitation for any month is 1/12 of (A)
in the case of an eligible individual who has self-only coverage under a high
deductible health plan as of the first day of such month, $2,250. (B) in the
case of an eligible individual who has family coverage under a high deductible
health plan as of the first day of such month, $4,500." These dollar amounts
are indexed (26 U.S.C. § 223(g)); Rev. Proc. 2023-23 section 3.04 gives, for
calendar year 2024, "$4,150" for self-only coverage and "$8,300" for family
coverage (`rp-23-23.pdf` p 2; `P.hsa_limit_self_only`, `P.hsa_limit_family`).
A filer eligible in all twelve months with one kind of coverage has twelve
equal months, so the limit is the annual figure.

"(3) Additional contributions for individuals 55 or older. (A) In general. In
the case of an individual who has attained age 55 before the close of the
taxable year, the applicable limitation under subparagraphs (A) and (B) of
paragraph (2) shall be increased by the additional contribution amount." The
additional contribution amount is $1,000 (`P.hsa_catch_up_55`).

Form 8889 instructions, line 3 (`i8889--2024.pdf` p 5): "If, at the end of
2024, you were age 55 or older and unmarried or married with self-only HDHP
coverage for the entire year, you can increase the amount determined in (3) or
(4) by $1,000 (the additional contribution amount)." and "Note. If you are
married and had family coverage at any time during the year, the additional
contribution amount is figured on line 7 and is not included on line 3."
DF follows this split between lines 3 and 7; the total on line 8 is the same.

```catala
scope Hsa:
  # DF: hsa.xml /filers/*/hsaBaseContributionLimit. DF's comment: partial-year
  # coverage would not have a $0 limit, "but we rely on KOs to ensure that
  # anyone reaching this calculation does have $0 limit".
  definition hsa_base_contribution_limit of role equals
    if (was_eligible_to_make_hsa_contributions_all_year of role)
       and (has_self_only_hdhp of role)
       and not hsa_married_filers_have_family_coverage
    then P.hsa_limit_self_only
    else if (was_eligible_to_make_hsa_contributions_all_year of role)
            and (is_covered_by_family_hdhp of role)
    then P.hsa_limit_family
    else $0
  # Form 8889 line 3. DF: hsa.xml /filers/*/hsaInitialContributionLimit
  definition hsa_initial_contribution_limit of role equals
    if has_made_contributions_to_hsa of role
    then R.round_dollar of
      (if ((was_eligible_to_make_hsa_contributions_all_year of role)
           and (age55_or_older of role)
           and (((is_covered_by_family_hdhp of role)
                 or (is_covered_by_self_only_hdhp of role))
                and not is_married))
          or ((was_eligible_to_make_hsa_contributions_all_year of role)
              and (age55_or_older of role)
              and (is_covered_by_self_only_hdhp of role) and is_married)
       then (hsa_base_contribution_limit of role) + P.hsa_catch_up_55
       else hsa_base_contribution_limit of role)
    else $0
  # Form 8889 line 4 is the Archer MSA amount, $0 here (ko_hsa_medical_savings_account_type).
  # Form 8889 line 5. DF: hsa.xml /filers/*/hsaContributionLimitLessMsaContributions
  definition hsa_contribution_limit_less_msa_contributions of role equals
    if has_made_contributions_to_hsa of role
    then hsa_initial_contribution_limit of role
    else $0
```

### Line 6: spouses with separate HSAs and family coverage

"(5) Special rule for married individuals. In the case of individuals who are
married to each other, if either spouse has family coverage ... the limitation
under paragraph (1) (after the application of subparagraph (A) and without
regard to any additional contribution amount under paragraph (3)) shall be
reduced by the aggregate amount paid to Archer MSAs of such spouses for the
taxable year, and after such reduction, shall be divided equally between them
unless they agree on a different division."

Form 8889 instructions, line 6 (`i8889--2024.pdf` p 7): "If you are treated as
having family coverage for each month, divide the amount on line 5 equally
between you and your spouse, unless you both agree on a different allocation
(such as allocating nothing to one spouse). Enter your allocable share on
line 6."

DF-BUG(12) candidate: Direct File never asks whether the spouses agree on a
division. `hsa.xml` /hsaPrimaryFilerAllocatedContributionLimit and
/hsaSecondaryFilerAllocatedContributionLimit (lines 2689 to 2786) assume an
agreement that gives the primary filer what the primary filer contributed
(contributions on lines 2 and 11 less line 7, capped at line 5) and the
secondary filer the rest. Without an agreement the law divides equally, so
this module divides equally. Where DF's allocation gives a larger deduction,
the difference shows as a `knownDivergence`.

```catala
scope Hsa:
  # DF: hsa.xml /filers/*/hasMetFamilyContributionLimitRule
  definition has_met_family_contribution_limit_rule of role equals
    hsa_married_filers_have_family_coverage and both_filers_have_hsa
    and (has_hdhp_coverage_all_year of role)
  # IRC 223(b)(5)(B)(ii), Form 8889 instructions line 6 (p 7): equal division.
  # DF-BUG(12) candidate: see above.
  definition hsa_allocated_contribution_limit of role equals
    (hsa_contribution_limit_less_msa_contributions of role) * 50%
  # Form 8889 line 6. DF: hsa.xml /filers/*/hsaContributionLimitLessAddition
  definition hsa_contribution_limit_less_addition of role equals
    if has_made_contributions_to_hsa of role
    then R.round_dollar of
      (if has_met_family_contribution_limit_rule of role
       then hsa_allocated_contribution_limit of role
       else hsa_contribution_limit_less_msa_contributions of role)
    else $0
```

### Line 7: additional contribution amount

Form 8889 line 7: "If you were age 55 or older at the end of 2024, married,
and you or your spouse had family coverage under an HDHP at any time during
2024, enter your additional contribution amount." Instructions p 7: "If items
(1) and (2) apply to all months during 2024, enter $1,000 on line 7."

```catala
scope Hsa:
  # Form 8889 line 7. DF: hsa.xml /filers/*/additionToHsaContributionLimit
  definition addition_to_hsa_contribution_limit of role equals
    if has_made_contributions_to_hsa of role
    then R.round_dollar of
      (if (was_eligible_to_make_hsa_contributions_all_year of role)
          and age55_or_older of role
          and (is_covered_by_family_hdhp of role) and is_married
       then P.hsa_catch_up_55
       else $0)
    else $0
```

### Lines 8 to 13: the total limit and the deduction

Form 8889, "8 Add lines 6 and 7", "9 Employer contributions made to your HSAs for
2024", "10 Qualified HSA funding distributions", "11 Add lines 9 and 10", "12
Subtract line 11 from line 8. If zero or less, enter -0-", "13 HSA deduction".
Instructions line 9 (`i8889--2024.pdf` p 7): employer contributions "should be
shown on Form W-2, box 12, code W". Instructions line 13 (p 8): "Generally,
enter the smaller of line 2 or line 12 on line 13 and on Schedule 1 (Form
1040), Part II, line 13." Instructions p 5: "Combine the amounts on line 13
of both Forms 8889 and enter this amount on Schedule 1 (Form 1040), line 13."

```catala
scope Hsa:
  # Line 9. DF: hsa.xml /filers/*/hsaContributionsW2sTotal
  definition hsa_contributions_w2s_total of role equals
    R.round_dollar of
      (if is_filing_status_mfj and is_secondary of role
       then secondary_filer_total_hsa_contributions_from_w2s
       else primary_filer_total_hsa_contributions_from_w2s)
  # Line 10. DF: hsa.xml /filers/*/hsaFundingDistributionsTotal is always $0:
  # funding distributions are not supported (ko_made_qualified_hsa_funding_distribution).
  definition hsa_funding_distributions_total of role equals $0
  # Line 11. DF: hsa.xml /filers/*/hsaEmployerContributionsAndFundingDistributionTotal
  definition hsa_employer_contributions_and_funding_distribution_total of role equals
    R.round_dollar of
      ((hsa_contributions_w2s_total of role)
       + (hsa_funding_distributions_total of role))
  # DF: hsa.xml /filers/*/hsaContributionsTotal
  definition hsa_contributions_total of role equals
    R.round_dollar of
      ((hsa_employer_contributions_and_funding_distribution_total of role)
       + (hsa_nonemployer_contributions_total of role))
  # Line 8. DF: hsa.xml /filers/*/hsaTotalContributionLimit
  definition hsa_total_contribution_limit of role equals
    if has_made_contributions_to_hsa of role
    then R.round_dollar of
      ((hsa_contribution_limit_less_addition of role)
       + (addition_to_hsa_contribution_limit of role))
    else $0
  # Line 12. DF: hsa.xml /filers/*/hsaContributionLimitLessLine11
  definition hsa_contribution_limit_less_line11 of role equals
    if has_made_contributions_to_hsa of role
    then Money.positive of
      ((hsa_total_contribution_limit of role)
       - (hsa_employer_contributions_and_funding_distribution_total of role))
    else $0
  # Line 13. DF: hsa.xml /filers/*/hsaTotalDeductibleAmount
  definition filer_hsa_total_deductible_amount of role equals
    if has_made_contributions_to_hsa of role
    then Money.min of
      (hsa_nonemployer_contributions_total of role),
      (hsa_contribution_limit_less_line11 of role)
    else $0
  # Schedule 1 line 13 / Form 1040 line 10. DF: hsa.xml /hsaTotalDeductibleAmount
  # (a Switch with no default when neither filer has contributions; the
  # Form 1040 reads it as $0 then, form_1040.catala_en line 374).
  definition hsa_total_deductible_amount equals
    filer_hsa_total_deductible_amount of Types.FilerRole.PrimaryFiler
    + filer_hsa_total_deductible_amount of Types.FilerRole.SecondaryFiler

  # Excess contributions, Form 8889 instructions line 13 (p 8): "if the amount
  # on line 2 is more than the amount on line 13, you or someone on your behalf
  # (or your employer) contributed more to your HSA than is allowable".
  # DF: hsa.xml /filers/*/hasExcessHsaContributions
  definition has_excess_hsa_contributions of role equals
    (hsa_nonemployer_contributions_total of role)
    > (filer_hsa_total_deductible_amount of role)
  # DF: hsa.xml /filers/*/hsaContributionLimitExceeded (line 2 + line 11 > line 8)
  definition hsa_contribution_limit_exceeded of role equals
    (has_made_contributions_to_hsa of role)
    and (hsa_contributions_total of role) > (hsa_total_contribution_limit of role)
  # DF: hsa.xml /filers/*/hsaContributionLimitExceededAmount
  definition hsa_contribution_limit_exceeded_amount of role equals
    (hsa_contributions_total of role) - (hsa_total_contribution_limit of role)
  # Excess contributions are taxed (IRC 4973) and need Form 5329; not supported.
  # DF: hsa.xml /flowHsaContributionsOverLimitKnockout
  rule ko_hsa_contributions_over_limit under condition
    (hsa_contribution_limit_exceeded of Types.FilerRole.PrimaryFiler)
    or (hsa_contribution_limit_exceeded of Types.FilerRole.SecondaryFiler)
  consequence fulfilled
```

## Form 8889 Part II: distributions

Form 8889 instructions, line 14a (`i8889--2024.pdf` p 8): "Enter the total
distributions you received in 2024 from all HSAs ... These amounts should be
shown on Form 1099-SA, box 1." Line 14b: "any distributions you received in
2024 that qualified as a rollover contribution to another HSA ... Also include
any excess contributions (and the earnings on those excess contributions)
included on line 14a that were withdrawn by the due date". Form 8889 line 14c
"Subtract line 14b from line 14a", line 15 "Qualified medical expenses paid
using HSA distributions", line 16 "Taxable HSA distributions. Subtract line 15
from line 14c. If zero or less, enter -0-."

DF models only distributions that are fully spent on qualified medical
expenses, so line 16 is `$0`; any 1099-SA with a larger modified distribution
is a knockout (`ko_hsa_unqualified_distributions`). The distribution code must
be 1 (`NormalDistribution`), and box 2 earnings and box 4 value on the date of
death must be zero. Those DF per-filer facts read the whole `/hsaDistributions`
collection and are gated by `/someFilerCanHaveDistribution`; they are
reproduced as "some distribution has the condition".

```catala
scope Hsa:
  # DF: hsa.xml /filers/*/hasHsaCanHaveDistribution
  definition has_hsa_can_have_distribution of role equals
    may_have_hsa_contributions of role
  # DF: hsa.xml /someFilerCanHaveDistribution
  definition some_filer_can_have_distribution equals
    (has_hsa_can_have_distribution of Types.FilerRole.PrimaryFiler)
    or (has_hsa_can_have_distribution of Types.FilerRole.SecondaryFiler)
  # DF: hsa.xml /primaryFilerHsaDistributions and /secondaryFilerHsaDistributions
  definition filer_items of role equals
    list of x among items such that
      (has_hsa_can_have_distribution of role) and x.filer = role
  # Line 14a. DF: hsa.xml /filers/*/totalHsaDistributions. DF sums the
  # writable gross distributions; the secondary filer's only on a joint return.
  definition total_hsa_distributions of role equals
    if is_filing_status_mfj or is_primary of role
    then R.round_dollar of
      (Money.sum of
        (map each x among filer_items of role to x.gross_distribution))
    else $0
  # DF: hsa.xml /filers/*/hsaRolloverTotal
  definition hsa_rollover_total of role equals
    if is_filing_status_mfj or is_primary of role
    then R.round_dollar of
      (Money.sum of
        (map each x among filer_items of role to x.distributions_rollover_amount))
    else $0
  # DF: hsa.xml /filers/*/hsaTotalExcessContributionsWithdrawnInTime
  definition hsa_total_excess_contributions_withdrawn_in_time of role equals
    if is_filing_status_mfj or is_primary of role
    then R.round_dollar of
      (Money.sum of
        (map each x among filer_items of role to
          x.withdrawn_excess_contributions_amount))
    else $0
  # Line 14b. DF: hsa.xml /filers/*/hsaRolloversAndTimelyWithdrawals
  definition hsa_rollovers_and_timely_withdrawals of role equals
    (hsa_total_excess_contributions_withdrawn_in_time of role)
    + (hsa_rollover_total of role)
  # DF: hsa.xml /filers/*/hsaNetDistributionAmount (undefined, shown as $0,
  # when line 14a and line 14b are both $0)
  definition hsa_net_distribution_amount of role equals
    if (total_hsa_distributions of role)
       + (hsa_rollovers_and_timely_withdrawals of role) > $0
    then Money.positive of
      ((total_hsa_distributions of role)
       - (hsa_rollovers_and_timely_withdrawals of role))
    else $0
  # Line 14c. DF: hsa.xml /filers/*/hsaCalculatedDistributionAmount (left blank,
  # shown as $0, when the net amount and line 14a are both $0)
  definition hsa_calculated_distribution_amount of role equals
    hsa_net_distribution_amount of role
  # Line 15. DF: hsa.xml /filers/*/hsaQualifiedMedExpenses
  definition hsa_qualified_med_expenses of role equals
    if is_filing_status_mfj or is_primary of role
    then R.round_dollar of
      (Money.sum of
        (map each x among filer_items of role to x.qualified_med_expenses))
    else $0
  # Line 16. DF: hsa.xml /filers/*/taxableHsaDistributionTotal and
  # /filers/*/hsaCalculatedTaxableHsaDistributionTotal are the constant $0
  # (DF's comment: it "relies on hsa-ko-unqualified-distributions knocking out
  # distributions where writableGrossDistribution does not equal
  # writableQualifiedMedExpenses"). Form 8889 line 16 is line 14c less line 15,
  # not below zero; ko_hsa_unqualified_distributions guarantees that is $0.
  definition hsa_calculated_taxable_hsa_distribution_total of role equals $0
  # DF: hsa.xml /filers/*/hasHsaDistributions
  definition has_hsa_distributions of role equals
    (has_hsa_can_have_distribution of role)
    and (total_hsa_distributions of role) > $0

  # DF: hsa.xml /flowKnockoutEarningsOnExcessContributions
  rule ko_earnings_on_excess_contributions under condition
    some_filer_can_have_distribution
    and exists x among items such that x.has_earnings_on_excess_contributions
  consequence fulfilled
  # DF: hsa.xml /flowKnockoutHsaDistributionCode (via
  # /flowKnockoutHsaDistributionsNotNormal)
  rule ko_hsa_distribution_code under condition
    some_filer_can_have_distribution
    and exists x among items such that x.code_is_not_normal
  consequence fulfilled
  # DF: hsa.xml /flowKnockoutHsaUnqualifiedDistributions
  rule ko_hsa_unqualified_distributions under condition
    some_filer_can_have_distribution
    and exists x among items such that x.has_unqualified_distribution
  consequence fulfilled
  # DF: hsa.xml /flowKnockoutHsaDistributionFMV
  rule ko_hsa_distribution_fmv under condition
    some_filer_can_have_distribution
    and exists x among items such that x.has_fmv_on_date_of_death
  consequence fulfilled
  # DF: hsa.xml /hsaDistributions/secondaryFilerUsedWithoutMFJ
  rule ko_hsa_distributions_secondary_filer_used_without_mfj under condition
    some_filer_can_have_distribution and not is_filing_status_mfj
    and exists x among items such that x.filer = Types.FilerRole.SecondaryFiler
  consequence fulfilled
  # DF: hsa.xml /hsaDistributions/*/hasDistributionsWithoutHsaActivity
  rule ko_has_hsa_distributions_without_activity under condition
    some_filer_can_have_distribution
    and not ko_hsa_distributions_secondary_filer_used_without_mfj
    and exists x among items such that
      not (has_hsa_can_have_distribution of x.filer)
  consequence fulfilled

  # DF: hsa.xml /knockoutNoPaymentsHsaDistribution: no taxable income and no
  # credits or payments, but HSA distributions.
  rule ko_no_payments_hsa_distribution under condition
    not paid_estimated_taxes_or_from_last_year
    and knockout_has_no_payments_or_credits
    and tax_exempt_interest = $0 and pensions_and_annuities = $0
    and social_security_benefits = $0
    and ((has_hsa_distributions of Types.FilerRole.PrimaryFiler)
         or (has_hsa_distributions of Types.FilerRole.SecondaryFiler))
  consequence fulfilled
```

## Who files Form 8889, and the lines of each form

```catala
scope Hsa:
  # DF: hsa.xml /numberOfFilersRequiredToFileForm8889
  definition number_of_filers_required_to_file_form_8889 equals
    (if (has_made_contributions_to_hsa of Types.FilerRole.PrimaryFiler)
        or (has_hsa_distributions of Types.FilerRole.PrimaryFiler)
     then 1 else 0)
    + (if (has_made_contributions_to_hsa of Types.FilerRole.SecondaryFiler)
          or (has_hsa_distributions of Types.FilerRole.SecondaryFiler)
       then 1 else 0)
  # DF: hsa.xml /requiresForm8889
  rule requires_form_8889 under condition
    number_of_filers_required_to_file_form_8889 > 0
  consequence fulfilled

  definition form_8889 of role equals
    Form8889 {
      -- line_1_family: (has_made_contributions_to_hsa of role)
                        and (is_covered_by_family_hdhp of role)
      -- line_1_self_only: (has_made_contributions_to_hsa of role)
                           and (is_covered_by_self_only_hdhp of role)
      -- line_2: hsa_nonemployer_contributions_total of role
      -- line_3: hsa_initial_contribution_limit of role
      -- line_5: hsa_contribution_limit_less_msa_contributions of role
      -- line_6: hsa_contribution_limit_less_addition of role
      -- line_7: addition_to_hsa_contribution_limit of role
      -- line_8: hsa_total_contribution_limit of role
      -- line_9: hsa_contributions_w2s_total of role
      -- line_11: hsa_employer_contributions_and_funding_distribution_total of role
      -- line_12: hsa_contribution_limit_less_line11 of role
      -- line_13: filer_hsa_total_deductible_amount of role
      -- line_14a: total_hsa_distributions of role
      -- line_14b: hsa_rollovers_and_timely_withdrawals of role
      -- line_14c: hsa_calculated_distribution_amount of role
      -- line_15: hsa_qualified_med_expenses of role
      -- line_16: hsa_calculated_taxable_hsa_distribution_total of role
    }
```

## Unsupported

The 19 DF facts that `flow.xml` (lines 77 to 95) feeds into
`/flowIsKnockedOut`, in that file's order, and the two block-submission
validations of `hsa.xml`.

```catala
scope Hsa:
  rule unsupported under condition
    ko_no_payments_hsa_distribution
    or ko_hsa_medical_savings_account_type
    or ko_hsa_distribution_code
    or ko_other_coverage_part_of_year
    or ko_other_coverage_whole_year
    or ko_earnings_on_excess_contributions
    or ko_hsa_testing_period_additional_income_yes
    or ko_hsa_unqualified_distributions
    or ko_hsa_distribution_fmv
    or ko_marital_change_affects_contribution_limit
    or ko_mfs_line6_check
    or ko_hsa_contributions_over_limit
    or ko_hsa_excess_contributions
    or ko_contribution_summary_none_allowed
    or ko_hdhp_coverage_status_not_needed
    or ko_not_enrolled_in_hdhp
    or ko_made_qualified_hsa_funding_distribution
    or ko_hsa_coverage
    or ko_filer_is_dependent_and_contributes_to_hsa
    or ko_has_hsa_distributions_without_activity
    or ko_hsa_distributions_secondary_filer_used_without_mfj
  consequence fulfilled
```
